course: dictionary
lesson: 6448
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word nanny is a good example. «Her nanny, Gabi, picks her up every day, plaits her hair and knows her favourite biscuit.» Here a nanny is a person paid to look after children in their home, because she picks the child up and plaits her hair.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Nanny and Grandad are coming for tea» uses the word for a grandmother, because Grandad is in the same sentence. A nanny can also be a female goat, as in «The nanny goat had two kids.» Here the goat clue tells you the meaning.
explain: Some meanings are not neutral. «Nanny state» is an informal phrase, and people use it to complain that a government makes too many rules. When you read a word you know, check: which meaning fits this sentence, and what clues tell me?
fact: A nanny is a person paid to look after a family's children in the family's home.
fact: In the UK, many children call their grandmother Nanny or Nan.
fact: A nanny goat is a female goat; a male goat is a billy goat.
fact: «Nanny state» is informal and critical: it means a government that people think makes too many rules.
fact: The same word can have several meanings, so always check the clues in the sentence.
exercise: «Her nanny, Gabi, picks her up every day, plaits her hair and knows her favourite biscuit.» What is a nanny in this sentence? | A police officer | A goat with kids | *A person who looks after the child | A kind of biscuit
exercise: What is a nanny goat? | *A female goat | A baby goat | A farm dog | A male goat
exercise: «A nanny helps a busy parent; it does not mean the parent doesn't love the child.» What does this sentence tell us? | *Having a nanny does not mean a parent doesn't love the child | Parents never need any help | A nanny replaces a parent's love | Nannies only look after goats
test: Lily calls her gran «Nanny». Who is Nanny? | *Her grandmother | A goat | A teacher from school | A babysitter from next door
test: What does «nanny state» mean? | A happy place for children to play | *A government that people think makes too many rules | A country full of goats | A place where nannies live with children
exam: Which meaning of nanny fits «Nanny and Grandad are coming for tea»? | A government with too many rules | *A child's word for grandmother | A female goat | A person paid to look after children at home
